# Repo-root-only dataset/output/env directories. Anchored with a leading
# slash so each pattern matches ONLY that exact top-level path — NOT any
# directory of the same name at any depth. Without the leading slash, git
# treats e.g. "data/" as matching "data/" *or* "src/data/" *or*
# "anything/data/" anywhere in the tree. That exact bug silently excluded
# the real src/data/ source package (build_splits.py, preprocess_raw.py,
# etc.) from every commit — see HANDOFF.md / the 2026-08 restructure notes.
/data_raw/
/Dataset/
/data/
/preprocessed/
/embeddings/
/checkpoints/
/logs/
/demos/
/CelebDF/
/DFDC/
/FaceForensics/
/venv/
/env/
/.deepfake/
/conda_env/
/ensemble_features/
/.vscode/

# Tool-generated cache directories: intentionally NOT anchored — these are
# meant to be excluded wherever they appear (a venv, a subpackage, etc.),
# unlike the project-specific directories above.
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb_checkpoints
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.so
*.env
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.pth
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.log
*.tmp
*.cache
debug_*.json
/KNOWLEDGE_BASE.md

# Generated results (see results/README.md for the expected schema) —
# tracked README stays, generated metrics.json does not. Anchored for the
# same reason as the block above — no nested "results/" dir exists in this
# repo today, but there's no reason to leave the same latent risk in place.
/results/metrics.json
/results/leakage_report.json

# Python packaging / virtual envs
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/